ine_hash</code> one key for "the same pipeline again": a registry, a cache, an orchestrator task State <code>state</code> <code>StatefulOperator</code>, <code>CarryState</code> state carried across calls: time steps, training, streams Protocols <code>protocols</code> <code>Predictor</code>, <code>FittableTransformer</code> accepting a model without importing its library <p>The sister packages build on this core: time stepping and data assimilation in <code>pipekit-cycle</code>, training in <code>pipekit-train</code>, the model registry in <code>pipekit-experiment</code>, benchmarks in <code>pipekit-evaluate</code>, Array API dispatch in <code>pipekit-array</code>, JAX models in <code>pipekit-jax</code>.</p> <p>The examples share one small operator:</p> <pre><code>from pipekit import Operator


class Scale(Operator):
    """x ↦ a · x."""

    def __init__(self, factor: float) -&gt; None:
        self.factor = factor  # stored under its argument's name → its config

    def _apply(self, x):
        return x * self.factor
